 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? That's usually due to worn out bearings. You can swap them with new ones, or keep pushing the bike with your foot until you reach top. Sadly no, it's not strong enough for bike chains. You need special grease or a full replacement kit. Pop off the old bearings with a sharp blade, then use a tool to push the new ones in. Comes with its own tool, so you don't damage anything. Clean it with bike cleaner, then grease it with the stuff comes with. Not really, it' worth doing every few years to keep the chain from getting too loud.",
